# Allowlist, not a denylist. The repo holds files that must never enter a
# build context — .env files, apf.env, kickbase-api.md with its live bearer
# tokens — and those are only gitignored, so they do sit on disk. Ignoring
# everything and naming what the build needs means a new secret file cannot
# leak into an image layer by being forgotten here.
*

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!index.html
!vite.config.ts
!tsconfig.json
!tsconfig.app.json
!tsconfig.node.json
!src
!public

# Copied into the runtime stage.
!nginx.conf
